  "notes": "Huge refactor (58+ files) that replaces mock models with real HuggingFace models. Head's SleeperDetector.initialize always calls load_model_for_detection(download_if_missing=True); the base paths also call from_pretrained. There is no cached model and the network is off. Most evaluator.py changes fill in methods that only raise NotImplementedError in base, and on head they depend on the new head-only ModelInterface. Most other files are new modules. The only offline-runnable change is ProbeDetector.train_probe/detect: a workload for it (scikit-learn installed in both venvs) runs on both sides in about 5-6 s but reaches only 3.8% of changed lines on head and 6.5% on base, against the 50% minimum, and outputs differ because the default regularisation and solver changed. Reaching more would need a network download or replacing the detector/model classes under test."
